    readTime: "5 min read",
    heroImage: smarvy150,
    tags: ["Dubai", "Showroom", "Buying Guide"],
    isFeatured: false,
    contentBlocks: [
      { type: "paragraph", content: "Browsing lighting catalogs online is useful for initial research, but it cannot replace the experience of seeing fixtures in person. A showroom visit lets you evaluate the true quality of light output, compare color temperatures side by side, test dimming and control systems, and assess build quality firsthand." },
      { type: "heading2", content: "Before You Visit: What to Prepare" },
      { type: "paragraph", content: "Bring your architectural floor plans or at least rough room dimensions. This allows the showroom team to provide relevant recommendations based on your actual ceiling heights, room sizes, and intended use. If you have mood boards or reference images, bring those too — they help communicate your design intent more effectively than verbal descriptions." },
      { type: "paragraph", content: "Make a note of any specific technical requirements: IP rating for outdoor or wet areas, dimming protocol preferences (DALI, Casambi, or 0-10V), voltage requirements, and any building code constraints. Having these details ready prevents wasted time and ensures the recommendations you receive are genuinely suitable for your project." },
      { type: "heading2", content: "What to Evaluate at the Showroom" },
      { type: "paragraph", content: "**Color temperature.** The difference between 2700K and 3000K looks minor on a specification sheet but is clearly visible when you see both options next to each other. Ask to see fixtures at different color temperatures operating simultaneously so you can compare them under the same conditions." },
      { type: "paragraph", content: "**Beam quality.** Look at the light pattern on the wall or ceiling. Is it smooth and even, or does it show rings, shadows, or hot spots? Premium fixtures produce clean, uniform beams with smooth transitions at the edges." },
      { type: "paragraph", content: "**Build quality.** Pick up the fixture and feel the weight. Quality fixtures use solid aluminum bodies with machined finishes. Cheap alternatives use thin stamped steel or plastic that warps under heat." },
      { type: "heading2", content: "After Your Visit: Next Steps" },
      { type: "paragraph", content: "Request a written quotation that includes product specifications, quantities, unit prices, delivery timelines, warranty terms, and installation scope (if applicable). A professional lighting company will follow up with a detailed proposal within a few business days." },
      { type: "callout", content: "Visit the Credence Lighting showroom at Dubai Investment Park 1 to see premium fixtures in working displays. Book an appointment for a personalized consultation with our lighting specialists." }
    ],
    seoMetadata: {
      title: "Visiting a Lighting Showroom in Dubai · Credence",
      description: "How to prepare for a lighting showroom visit in Dubai. What to bring, what to evaluate, and how to compare fixtures effectively."
    }
